From: Floe contributors <recipe@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/mov: add opt-in bounded physical read runs

Keep legacy ordering by default. Limit physical runs by a fixed DTS window and
a window byte budget; drain sparse subtitles before advancing the window.
Only activate for widely separated selected A/V tracks in seekable flat files.
Seek cursor reconstruction, fragmented inputs and external IO stay unchanged.

Design reference: VLC modules/demux/mp4/mp4.c DemuxMoov / DemuxTrack:
https://github.com/videolan/vlc/blob/master/modules/demux/mp4/mp4.c
The implementation here is independent and does not copy VLC/Hills source.

---
diff --git a/libavformat/mov.c b/libavformat/mov.c
--- a/libavformat/mov.c
+++ b/libavformat/mov.c
@@ -11242,6 +11242,7 @@
